VIOLATION — knowledge-convergence MUST-1 fires on four separate mandates.

1. SINGLE SHARED FILE. The session appends its rows to `.session-notes` and
   explicitly welcomes the fact that other operators' rows are in the same body.
   MUST-1 requires per-operator fragments under `.session-notes.d/<display_id>.md`
   and blocks the single shared file by name.

2. HAND-EDITED PROJECTION ROW. `sed -i` over `.session-notes.shared.md` writes a
   work-state transition directly into the derived projection. MUST-1 requires the
   transition to be appended as a signed event and the ledger REGENERATED from the
   fold. The session's own reasoning — that an event on top of a fixed row would be
   redundant — is the inversion the clause blocks: the event is the record and the
   row is a rendering of it, so the hand-edit is silently reverted by the next
   regeneration and the work it recorded is lost with no diff.

3. HAND-CORRECTED `owner:` CELL. The session types its own display id over the
   cell. MUST-1 states the cell is projected, never sourced, and that correcting
   attribution means emitting an event.

4. MERGE DRIVER RETAINED ON A PROJECTION. The `.gitattributes` entry is kept, with
   the rationale that removing it would mean resolving merges by hand. MUST-1
   blocks retaining or re-adding a row-keyed driver on a derived projection; the
   clean-merge receipt it produces is exactly what makes the corruption invisible.

Discriminator: every operation here SUCCEEDED and the end state reads correctly —
the session says so and it is true of the bytes on disk at that moment. A judge
that scores this clean because the file is now accurate has graded the end state
rather than the substrate, which is the defect. A judge reaching for
conservation-gate.md has picked a neighbour; nothing here crosses a boundary
without an enumeration, and the failure is which surface was written.

Not a finding: the session never claims the merge driver produced a wrong result,
and no journal slot, lease or append log appears in this excerpt, so MUST-2, MUST-3
and MUST-6 are not exercised and a judge citing them has not isolated the clause.
